{
  "react": {
    "observe": "GoldenWhale's NOVA token launched with a $60K seed and public 10x exit-trigger commitment. Retail (HappyTrader, DiamondHands) took small test positions. LiquidKiller, LeverageKing, CryptoGuru, BearKing, ShadowTrader are all skeptical, waiting for either the $0.01 trigger or unrelated-wallet buying before engaging. The NOVA pool itself shows liquidity=3.4M and price ~$0.001 — consistent with launch price, no pump yet. Custom synthetic pools (BTCUSDT3/ETHUSDT2/SOLUSDT4) remain dead/thin liquidity, no real arb. Oracle prices: ETH 1786.26, SOL 75.26, BTC 62694.83 — nothing unusual. My prior BTC accumulation (many small buys) plus SOL/ETH top-ups have left me with reasonable spot exposure already.",
    "think": "NOVA is the only live catalyst. Creator holds majority supply, self-reported exit trigger is unenforceable — classic rug setup. The room consensus (correctly) is skepticism. As an arbitrageur, I don't want to be the retail bagholder buying a creator-seeded pump. However, there IS a possible small edge: if NOVA pumps toward $0.01 on retail FOMO, I could take a tiny speculative position now (cheap, ~$0.001) and exit fast on any spike, before the whale's exit-trigger hits — essentially front-running the retail wave with minimal capital at risk, since downside is capped at my small stake. But this isn't 'arbitrage', it's speculation, and my mandate is capital preservation with low-risk profit only. Given majority supply concentration, real risk of zero liquidity on exit. Better to stay disciplined and continue the low-risk beta-tracking top-up strategy that has kept me slightly positive, while directing this cycle's mandatory trade toward ETH since BTC and SOL got recent attention.",
    "plan": "Continue rotation discipline: this cycle top up ETH modestly (~$100 notional) since SOL was last rotation target. Avoid NOVA entirely — no structural edge, pure gamble on an unenforceable creator promise. Keep watching LiquidKiller's SOL short thesis (liquidation ~19% above spot) as the most credible catalyst; if SOL approaches that level, consider a small counter-position. Also keep monitoring NOVA pool price — if it approaches $0.01 trigger with genuine third-party volume (not creator-seeded), reassess for a very small fade-the-pump short opportunity via spot sell after any spike, but not before confirmed movement.",
    "trades": [
      {"action": "buy_spot", "pair": "ETHUSDT", "quantity": 0.05}
    ]
  },
  "trades": [
