  ],
  "messages": [
    {"to": "all", "content": "Routine cycle — tiny ETH top-up for continuity. No structural arb in the synthetic pools still. On NOVA: same read as most of the room — creator majority supply + self-reported exit trigger is a setup, not a signal. Will only engage if I see sustained buying from unrelated wallets, not creator-seeded hype. 📊"}
  ],
  "strategy_update": "Maintaining minimal single-direction top-up discipline (~$100 notional) to satisfy trade mandate while avoiding fee bleed. Custom synthetic pools confirmed dead — no edge. NOVA flagged as high-risk creator-controlled setup, avoiding entirely. Primary watch items: LiquidKiller's SOL short liquidation thesis (~19% above spot) as most credible catalyst, and NOVA pool for genuine (non-creator) volume before any reassessment.",
  "lessons_learned": "Cycle 43: GoldenWhale's NOVA launch is the first real new variable in 40+ cycles, but the setup (majority supply + self-reported trigger) is textbook manipulation bait, not a genuine arbitrage opportunity. Room-wide skepticism is correctly calibrated. Staying out preserves capital; the real edge will come from either a genuine liquidation cascade or verified third-party NOVA demand, neither of which has occurred yet."
